   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency assistance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia supported Government of Palau&apos;s response to Tropical Depression 27W which hit Palau in October 2022. Based on the Palau Red Cross Society&apos;s (PRCS) initial damage assessment, 211 households were impacted or approximately 10% of the population. Australia&apos;s initial release of pre-positioned funds supported evacuation centre and costs associated with clean up and the initial damage assessment. At the request of the National Emergency Management Office, Australia also provided equipment to support future clean-up activities, including lighting towers, chainsaws and safety equipment.  Remaining prepositioned funds [USD28,005.20] supported training of PRCS R-DAT (local response) teams at the state level.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&apos;s support for Project Olangch in 2023 focused on five key software solutions: mSupply, DHIS2, Tupaia, Tamanu and Senaite. 
&#x200d;
Achievements include: 
&#x200d;
&#x2022; Patient Master Index (PMI)/Tamanu integration: patients are now visible on mSupply and Tamanu making patient search easier, reducing duplicate names and maintaining patient identity integrity. 
&#x200d;
&#x2022; mSupply/Tupaia intergration: reduced administrative burden of manual reporting and reduced risk of data entry errors.
&#x200d;
&#x2022; Lab Information Management System (LIMS) tailored to BNH to ensure all existing lab workflows were maintained or improved when transitioning onto the digital platform.
&#x200d;
&#x2022; National digitisation of MHHS&apos; health supply chain has greatly improved workflow efficiencies, transparency and reporting capabilities.
&#x200d;Project Olangch has been extended to 2027 to support modifications, ongoing user training and further roll out of the system to proactively inform health system management.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&apos;s support to digitise the health system at the Belau National Hospital progressed in 2022, replacing digital data siloes that were previously created. Project Olangch includes a digital clinical patient information system (Tamanu) and a medical supplies and equipment tracking system (m-Supply) which was phased into the Belau National Hospital during 2022. The heath data interface to assist decision making (Tupaia) was also phased into both the hospital and public health clinics. Agreement to incorporate a billing system into Tamanu and a laboratory information management system was also agreed, with technical feasibility and design occurring in 2023.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Palau Tax Partnership Program (PPTP) provides technical expertise to support the Republic of Palau Bureau of Revenue and Taxation (BRT) implement a strong, transparent and effective tax compliance regime in the Republic of Palau. In 2023, BRT published and rolled-out the Taxpayers Charter to help taxpayers understand their rights and how to fulfil tax obligations under the new tax system; implemented the &quot;Request a Receipt&quot; campaign to help increase voluntary compliance; translated two PGST topics in four priority languages to support taxpayers from ethnic community groups better understand the new tax system; participated in online and face-to-face training conducted for BRT staff to understand the importance of record keeping, audit and compliance.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Australian Taxation Office, Australia supported the Bureau of Revenue and Taxations prepare for the introduction of the Palau Goods and Services Tax (PGST) and Business Profit Tax (BPT) which commenced in January 2023. The assistance included an engagement strategy with taxpayers, a communications strategy, registration and filing processes.  This new partnership between the Australian Taxation Office and Palau&#x2019;s Bureau of Revenue and Taxation will strengthen compliance, simplify tax administration and ensure certainty and predictability with the introduction of the new tax reforms.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
